 "post": {
  "title": "Why One Insult Beats Ten Compliments #shorts",
  "description": "Arthur got ten compliments and one criticism, and at 2 AM he's replaying the criticism. Psychologists call this negativity bias: bad events weigh more than good ones (Baumeister et al., 'Bad Is Stronger Than Good', 2001; Rozin & Royzman, 2001). #psychology #shorts #overthinking",
